; TRACKED-KNOWN PANIC (a committed `PANIC` row in the catalog snapshot, per its header) — a table
; whose DOMAIN is a NAMED recursive union, with the cycle rooted so the table registers FIRST.
;
; `register_rust_struct` synthesizes the keys-list wasm wrapper from the domain at registration time,
; naming it through `name_as_wasm_array_ct` -> `directly_wasm_exposable_ct` -> `is_enum`. Rooting the
; holder at the UNION (`u_holder = [u_val]`) makes dep ordering register `u_map` before `u_val`
; exists as a struct, so `is_enum` finds the ident in neither `rust_structs` nor `generic_instances`
; and its assertion aborts generation. Reproduces under `--wasm=false` too: the synthesis runs on the
; parse walk, not on the wasm pass.
;
; The COLLECTION-rooted spelling of the same three rules generates and compiles cleanly on both
; faces — it is the `key_` block of tests/recursive-collection-ref/input.cddl, with the wasm half
; pinned by `recursive_union_keyed_table_mints_its_keys_list_under_wasm`. That pairing is what makes
; this fixture's variable the ROOTING, not the union-keyed shape itself. Single-rule spellings that
; inline the table as a union arm (`tmd = { * tmd => tmd } / int`) also generate.
;
; The fix route is the one this class already took once: defer the mint past the point where the
; domain resolves, as `finalize_generic_table_keys_lists` does for generic-collection instances.
; Tracked by the "Recursive-map-KEY limitation" entry in tests/TESTING_ROADMAP.md. When it lands,
; this row flips to `ok` in the catalog snapshot and the fixture becomes an ordinary regression pin.
u_holder = [u_val]
u_val = u_map / int / bytes / text
u_map = { * u_val => u_val }
